# ============================================================
# InfraReaper Trivy Vulnerability Suppression Policy (.trivyignore)
# ============================================================
# Documents and suppresses known upstream vulnerabilities inherited
# from the official Microsoft Azure CLI base image (mcr.microsoft.com/azure-cli).
#
# Threat Modeling & Risk Assessment:
# 1. The scanner is a batch CronJob executing inside an isolated K8s namespace.
# 2. It has no inbound network listeners, ingress ports, or external attack surfaces.
# 3. All identified CVEs reside in Microsoft's internal Python CLI virtualenv or OS base.
# 4. These findings are tracked and accepted upstream until Microsoft publishes updated base images.
# ============================================================

# --- Azure Linux OS Packages (Expat, OpenSSL, PCRE2, Python3) ---
# Expat XML parser vulnerabilities (InfraReaper only handles JSON payloads)
CVE-2026-77214
CVE-2026-93990

# PCRE2 regex out-of-bounds write (Scanner uses internal jq/bash regex)
CVE-2026-86145

# OpenSSL TLS/DTLS/QUIC issues (Scanner only makes standard HTTPS calls to ARM & SendGrid)
CVE-2026-72897
CVE-2026-84782
CVE-2026-84784

# Python 3 system runtime certificate list & SSLContext
CVE-2026-115557
CVE-2026-19445
CVE-2026-19553

# --- Azure CLI Python Virtualenv Packages (/usr/lib/az) ---
# PyJWT: Authentication bypass on JWT verification (Scanner does not verify or decode external JWTs)
CVE-2026-102268
CVE-2026-102266
CVE-2026-102267
CVE-2026-102271
CVE-2026-102272
CVE-2026-102273
GHSA-pxh4-856f-4h89

# certifi: Compromised intermediate CA in bundle
GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2

# cryptography: PKCS#7 & path building
CVE-2026-69247
CVE-2026-69249

# msgpack: Unpacker reuse and deserialization memory leak
CVE-2026-114613
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964

# setuptools: Path traversal in PackageIndex
CVE-2025-47273

# urllib3: Proxy override & chunk parser unbounded memory
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689
